details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene is captured from a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring all pancakes on the two plates are clearly visible with generous negative space surrounding them for circular cropping. The main pancake stack in the foreground is in sharp focus, while the second plate sits slightly blurred in the background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window to the left, creating subtle shadows and a gentle sheen on the warm blueberry jam. The setting is a cozy kitchen with a rustic, aged oak wood surface showing faint wear marks. Two simple, matte cream-colored ceramic plates are set on the wood. Each plate holds a small stack of three pancakes, each with a smooth, uniform, and tender golden-brown surface, slightly unevenly browned from the skillet. The pancakes are topped with a generous, thick, deep-purple blueberry and chia seed jam, with some berries still visibly bursting and whole. A few stray blueberries and a scattering of hemp hearts rest naturally on the wooden surface near the plates. A wooden spoon with a tiny bit of blueberry jam rests casually on the table. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric stack, a small drip of blueberry syrup on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the pancake edges. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few stray hemp hearts on the surface, a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
